## rc-calc | Calculus concept check | maths | 1 | calc1 | c1-px3
quiz 2 | What does f′(a) represent geometrically?
* The slope of the tangent line at x = a
o The area under f up to a
o The value of f at a
o The y-intercept
= The instantaneous rate of change.
> Next

quiz 3 | If f′(x) > 0 on an interval, f is…
* Increasing there
o Decreasing there
o Concave up
o Constant
= Positive slope means rising.
> Next

quiz 3 | What does the integral ∫ₐᵇ v(t) dt give, if v is velocity?
* Displacement
o Distance travelled (always)
o Acceleration
o Average speed
= Distance travelled is ∫|v| dt.
> Next

quiz 3 | Rolle's theorem: if f is continuous on [a, b], differentiable on (a, b), and f(a) = f(b), then…
* f′(c) = 0 for some c in (a, b)
o f is constant
o f(c) = 0 for some c
o f″(c) = 0 for some c
= A special case of the Mean Value Theorem.
> Next

quiz 3 | A function differentiable at a point must be…
* Continuous there
o Increasing there
o Zero there
o Twice differentiable there
= Differentiability implies continuity, not the reverse.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which is an antiderivative of 1/x for x > 0?
* ln x
o −1/x²
o x⁰
o eˣ
= d/dx ln x = 1/x.
> Next

quiz 4 | The second derivative test is inconclusive when…
* f″(c) = 0
o f″(c) > 0
o f″(c) < 0
o f′(c) ≠ 0
= Use the first derivative test instead.
> Next

quiz 3 | What does a definite integral of a rate give?
* The net change in the quantity
o The rate at the end
o The average rate
o Zero
= Net change theorem: ∫ₐᵇ F′(x) dx = F(b) − F(a).
> Next

quiz 4 | A series Σaₙ converges absolutely if…
* Σ|aₙ| converges
o aₙ → 0
o The partial sums are bounded
o It alternates
= Absolute convergence implies convergence.
> Next

quiz 4 | The radius of convergence of a power series can be found with…
* The ratio (or root) test
o The integral test
o The divergence test
o The comparison test only
= Apply it to |cₙ(x − a)ⁿ|.
> Next

quiz 4 | ∇f at a point is perpendicular to…
* The level curve (or surface) through that point
o The x-axis
o The tangent plane's normal
o Every other gradient
= It points in the direction of steepest increase.
> Next

quiz 4 | A vector field F is conservative on a simply connected region if…
* curl F = 0
o div F = 0
o F is constant
o |F| = 1
= Then F = ∇φ for some potential φ.
> Next

quiz 4 | The Jacobian for polar coordinates is…
* r
o 1
o r²
o sin θ
= dA = r dr dθ.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which theorem relates a line integral around a closed curve to a double integral over the region inside it?
* Green's theorem
o Divergence theorem
o Fundamental theorem of calculus
o Fubini's theorem
= ∮(P dx + Q dy) = ∬(Q_x − P_y) dA.
> Next

quiz 4 | The divergence theorem relates…
* Flux through a closed surface to the volume integral of the divergence
o Circulation to curl
o Area to perimeter
o Slope to area
= ∯ F·dS = ∭ ∇·F dV.
> Physics concept check next

## rc-phys1 | Mechanics concept check | physics | 1 | phys1 | p1-px3
quiz 2 | Newton's first law is also called the law of…
* Inertia
o Acceleration
o Action and reaction
o Gravitation
= Objects keep their velocity unless a net force acts.
> Next

quiz 3 | Momentum is conserved when…
* No net external force acts on the system
o Kinetic energy is conserved
o Objects stick together
o Friction is present
= Momentum is conserved in all collisions of an isolated system.
> Next

quiz 3 | The area under a force–displacement graph gives…
* Work done
o Power
o Momentum
o Acceleration
= W = ∫F dx.
> Next

quiz 3 | The area under a force–time graph gives…
* Impulse (change in momentum)
o Work
o Energy
o Power
= J = ∫F dt = Δp.
> Next

quiz 3 | For an object in uniform circular motion, the net force points…
* Toward the centre
o Along the velocity
o Outward
o It's zero
= Centripetal force: mv²/r.
> Next

quiz 3 | What quantity is conserved when no external torque acts?
* Angular momentum
o Linear momentum
o Kinetic energy
o Angular velocity
= L = Iω stays constant; ω can change if I does.
> Next

quiz 4 | In SHM, where is speed greatest?
* At the equilibrium position
o At the extremes
o Halfway to the extreme
o Speed is constant
= All energy is kinetic at equilibrium.
> Next

quiz 4 | A conservative force is one where…
* Work done is independent of path
o Energy is always lost
o It's always attractive
o It acts only on moving objects
= Gravity and springs: yes. Friction: no.
> Next

quiz 4 | Parallel axis theorem: I about a parallel axis at distance d equals…
* I_cm + Md²
o I_cm − Md²
o I_cm × d
o Md²
= From the centre-of-mass axis.
> Next

quiz 4 | In the Lagrangian formalism, L equals…
* T − V
o T + V
o V − T
o pq̇ − H
= The Hamiltonian is T + V (for standard systems).
> E&M concept check next

## rc-phys2 | E&M concept check | physics | 1 | phys2 | p2-px2
quiz 2 | Electric field lines point from…
* Positive to negative charge
o Negative to positive charge
o North to south
o High to low resistance
= They show the direction of force on a positive test charge.
> Next

quiz 3 | Inside a conductor in electrostatic equilibrium, the electric field is…
* Zero
o Maximum
o Uniform and non-zero
o Equal to the surface field
= Free charges rearrange until it vanishes.
> Next

quiz 3 | The unit of capacitance is the…
* Farad
o Henry
o Tesla
o Weber
= Henry is inductance; tesla is magnetic field; weber is flux.
> Next

quiz 3 | Kirchhoff's junction rule expresses conservation of…
* Charge
o Energy
o Momentum
o Mass
= The loop rule expresses energy conservation.
> Next

quiz 3 | A magnetic field exerts a force on a charge only if the charge is…
* Moving (not parallel to the field)
o Stationary
o Negative
o Inside a conductor
= F = qv × B.
> Next

quiz 4 | Lenz's law says induced current flows so as to…
* Oppose the change in magnetic flux
o Increase the flux
o Flow clockwise
o Maximise power
= A consequence of energy conservation.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which Maxwell equation says there are no magnetic monopoles?
* ∇·B = 0
o ∇·E = ρ/ε₀
o ∇×E = −∂B/∂t
o ∇×B = μ₀J + μ₀ε₀∂E/∂t
= Magnetic field lines have no sources or sinks.
> Next

quiz 4 | The displacement current term was added by…
* Maxwell
o Faraday
o Ampère
o Gauss
= It made the equations consistent with charge conservation and predicted EM waves.
> Next

quiz 4 | In an EM wave, E and B are…
* Perpendicular to each other and to the direction of travel
o Parallel to each other
o Parallel to the direction of travel
o 90° out of phase in vacuum
= In vacuum they're in phase, with E = cB.
> Next

quiz 4 | The time constant of an RL circuit is…
* L/R
o RC
o LR
o √(LC)
= Current rises to about 63% of its final value after one L/R.
> Modern physics concept check next

## rc-phys3 | Modern physics concept check | physics | 2 | phys3 | p3-px2
quiz 2 | Einstein's photoelectric equation is…
* KE_max = hf − φ
o E = mc²
o E = hf only
o λ = h/p
= φ is the work function of the metal.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which postulate is NOT part of special relativity?
* Mass is constant at all speeds
o The laws of physics are the same in all inertial frames
o The speed of light in vacuum is the same for all observers
= Relativistic energy and momentum depend on speed through γ.
> Next

quiz 3 | The Pauli exclusion principle applies to…
* Fermions
o Bosons
o Photons
o All particles
= No two identical fermions can share a quantum state.
> Next

quiz 3 | The second law of thermodynamics says the entropy of an isolated system…
* Never decreases
o Always stays constant
o Always decreases
o Is zero
= It increases in irreversible processes and stays constant in reversible ones.
> Next

quiz 4 | |ψ(x)|² gives…
* A probability density
o The particle's energy
o The particle's momentum
o The wave's speed
= Born's rule.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which quantity is quantised in the Bohr model?
* Angular momentum (in units of ħ)
o Linear momentum
o Mass
o Charge only
= L = nħ.
> Next

quiz 4 | A spin-½ particle has how many possible spin states along a measured axis?
* 2
o 1
o 3
o Infinite
= Up and down: m_s = ±½.
> Next

quiz 4 | Beta-minus decay turns…
* A neutron into a proton, emitting an electron and an antineutrino
o A proton into a neutron
o A nucleus into a helium nucleus
o An electron into a photon
= Mediated by the weak force (via a W⁻ boson).
> Next

quiz 4 | Which particle mediates the electromagnetic force?
* The photon
o The gluon
o The W boson
o The Higgs boson
= Gluons carry the strong force; W and Z the weak force.
> Next

quiz 5 | The commutator [x, p] equals…
* iħ
o 0
o ħ
o −iħ/2
= Canonical commutation relation.
> Concept checks complete
